I had a lot of fun with my archeologist in a recent game. I found a room
with a co-aligned altar, dug a criss-cross series of pits, made some
noise, then waited for the monsters to arrive. Most of them fell into
the pits and died immediately, and it was easy to finish the rest off.
Then, kick the corpses out of the pits (make sure that you have cleared
spaces with your pickaxe to kick them into), zig-zag your way to the
altar, and #offer them. It is also useful to kick out all the doors, then
put a pit immediately inside them. You can dart around the pits when
you enter a room running away from something, but most monsters will
fall into them. However, BEWARE the scroll of amnesia if you had dug
too elaborate a series of traps! Also, remember that after you dig a
pit, you will be stuck in it for a couple of turns.

		
